    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="eadf833d-7b0e-512e-a2e0-5cee7e79f421" activityNameId="ffb2199c-dc48-591c-b9a0-bbef1b171b0b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Bitumen adhesive compound, hot, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Bitumen adhesive compound, hot, at plant
The dataset is applicable in the construction building sector. Bitumen adhesive compound is used to protect roads and roofs against water intrusion.;
Synonyms: hot bonding compound, Heisskleber; 
UUID: 4ce7df0f-0ae5-3c01-b199-9bb44750207d
The dataset describes the production of hot bitumen adhesive compound. Included sub-processes are the heating of the bitumen compound, the infrastructure, the transport by road and rail as well as the disposal of the compound cuttings in a municipal incineration.
Location: The data of this dataset is extracted from literature and producer information. Some own calculations (e.g. energy input, waste heat) were made.
Technology: The technology involved is basically heating up the bitumen with a natural gas burner.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature, database 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4ce7df0f-0ae5-3c01-b199-9bb44750207d.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
